{
    "background_story": "Henley was a common goldeneye duck, scientifically known as Bucephala clangula. She lived in a cozy nest on the banks of a serene lake, surrounded by tall trees and lush vegetation. Henley was a bit of an oddity among her fellow ducks, as she had a fascination with the sounds of the human world. She would often sneak closer to the nearby village to listen to the clangs and clatters of the blacksmith's workshop. The rhythmic clangs of the hammer on the anvil mesmerized her, and she found herself synchronizing her quacks to the beat. The villagers, charmed by Henley's unique behavior, began to leave out treats for her, and she became a beloved fixture in the community. As the seasons changed, Henley's love for the clangula sounds remained constant, a testament to her curious and adventurous spirit.",
